Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.04,0:00:12.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,everyone I'm happy to have Dylan here.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.72,0:00:18.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,The first time I saw one of his videos was an interview when he talked about all the way up to
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.39,0:00:22.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,CPUs to talk about like neoclouds and why they have the right to exist and that was super interesting for me
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.97,0:00:28.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,because the theme of today is all like what are the new infrastructure primitives now that agents are here and so you
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.66,0:00:34.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,are tricking at that really well at that point why neoclouds are different from hyperscalers and why they should exist.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.58,0:00:36.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,So can you share any of that with us?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.88,0:00:37.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.48,0:00:41.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean um in the age of AI the hyperscalers were a little bit slow to move right Google
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.68,0:00:49.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Amazon Microsoft bit slow to move into AI and so a whole new crop of companies popped up and there was
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.15,0:00:55.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,a new low bar right there's no need for a lot of the complex software that Amazon Microsoft Google had built
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.39,0:01:00.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,up and a lot of this in fact slowed down AI right they had custom networks that were actually not that
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.99,0:01:07.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,great for AI they were more focused around reliability and storage traffic rather than you know doing an AllReduce across
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.53,0:01:12.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,the network or something like this so so there was a lot of things that these large cloud companies these hyper
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.36,0:01:19.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,scalers had that neoclouds could just skip right and and then build focused optimized solutions and deliver much lower cost
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.19,0:01:26.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,because they have much lower overhead right there's not 20,000 Google PMs sitting in a meeting at these neoclouds right
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.92,0:01:34.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,although some of them have started hiring Google PMs and slowed down the the the neoclouds they they they
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.52,0:01:39.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,just moved fast on energy they moved fast on bringing up GPU clusters and so they were able to carve out
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.93,0:01:44.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,a market right and then you know those are the early ones and then since then there have been a lot
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.49,0:01:51.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,more copycats or followers many who haven't succeeded many who are succeeding right it really is like a a battle of
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.77,0:01:56.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,like who's the most competent And so are all the cuz there's like I think you said there's like an order
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.04,0:02:03.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,there's like a 200 of these neoclouds or give or take right and so are there differentiations between them that
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.03,0:02:09.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,you see like are are some of them just copying the the sort of software stack that these first ones did
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.91,0:02:15.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,or they doing something else like anything that you've seen that have been successful and less successful across these neoclouds?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.59,0:02:20.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah so there's a variety of things that separate them right so we have something called ClusterMAX that
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.23,0:02:30.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,ranks all the neoclouds but we test for various things such as observability reliability networking security um orchestration all
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.77,0:02:36.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,these sorts of things are different right like does does someone test for their GPUs to be working properly
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.83,0:02:42.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,in when the GPUs are idle for a user right that's active health check or a passive health check hey
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.58,0:02:46.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,are the fans spinning at the right speed or are the you know is it drawing the right power
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.03,0:02:51.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,is there something wrong with the node is the is the network flapping or is anything problem problem with the
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.34,0:02:56.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,network is the performance there right like there's all these sorts of checks and tests because GPUs are unreliable um
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.87,0:03:02.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,there's all sorts of stuff around um the types of software you run on top of the GPU right many
